  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A student measuring the diameter of a pencil of circular cross-section with the help of a vernier scale records the following four readings&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>34</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>. The average of these four reading is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5375</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>&nbsp;and the standard deviation of the data is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>07395</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>. The average diameter of the pencil should therefore be recorded as :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "XjDky",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>.5375</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.0739</mo></mrow></mfenced><mi>mm</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
